---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Stamp from '../components/Stamp.astro';
import Term from '../components/Term.astro';
import { etprStages, edgeChain, gcsChain } from '../data/site.js';
---
<Base title="How it works" description="AVOFLARE's two chains: on the aircraft, CAN telemetry becomes a CanonicalTelemetryState that feeds the Edge AI; on the ground, GCS AI builds an engineering case for the engineer.">
  <PageHead title="Two chains, one engine" lead="On the aircraft, raw engine data becomes trusted telemetry and a local decision. On the ground, the same data becomes an engineering case a person signs. The aircraft never waits for the ground." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="arch" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: sensors and ECU send CAN frames to ETPR, which builds the CanonicalTelemetryState used by the Edge AI and Safety layer on the aircraft. The same state goes over the downlink to the ground station, where GCS AI, EIR and Sentinel prepare the case for the engineer.">
        <div class="arch-col">
          <p class="arch-h">Aircraft</p>
          <ol class="arch-list">
            <li>Sensors and <Term t="ECU" /></li>
            <li><Term t="CAN" /> bus · 17 message IDs, 60 signals</li>
            <li class="key"><Term t="ETPR" /></li>
            <li class="key"><Term t="CanonicalTelemetryState" /></li>
            <li>Edge AI</li>
            <li>Safety → aircraft response</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-link" aria-hidden="true"><span>downlink</span></div>
        <div class="arch-col">
          <p class="arch-h">Ground station</p>
          <ol class="arch-list">
            <li>Operational System</li>
            <li><Term t="EIR" /> · knowledge and history</li>
            <li><Term t="Sentinel" /> · controlled change</li>
            <li class="key">Engineer</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="etpr">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="display" style="font-size:var(--step-3)">ETPR: trusted telemetry</h2>
        <p><Stamp status="design" /> <span class="muted">CAN encoding and decoding: <Stamp status="impl" /></span></p>
        <p class="lead">A deterministic layer between the CAN bus and any AI. It knows nothing about models; it only makes every value correct, labelled and timed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <ol class="steps">
          {etprStages.map(([n, d]) => <li><strong>{n}</strong><span>{d}</span></li>)}
        </ol>
        <p>Every signal carries a status: <b>valid</b>, <b>missing</b> (never received), <b>stale</b> (too old for its own update rate), <b>reserved fault</b> or <b>out of range</b>. A 10 Hz signal goes stale after 300 ms; a 1 Hz signal after 3 s. The AI never has to guess why a value is bad.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="edge">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="display" style="font-size:var(--step-3)">Edge AI: decide on board</h2>
        <p><Stamp status="design" /></p>
        <p class="lead">Each stage has one job and hands a higher-level result to the next. Safety has the last word.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        {edgeChain.map(([n, d]) => <li><strong>{n === 'QR-DQN' ? <Term t="QR-DQN" label="Dueling Double Distributional QR-DQN" /> : n === 'EKF' ? <Term t="EKF" /> : n === 'Specialized SNN' ? <Term t="SNN" label="Specialized SNN" /> : n === 'PINN / Lite Digital Twin' ? <Term t="PINN" label="PINN / Lite Digital Twin" /> : n}</strong><span>{d}</span></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="gcs">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="display" style="font-size:var(--step-3)">GCS AI: build the engineering case</h2>
        <p><Stamp status="design" /></p>
        <p class="lead">Not a black-box failure predictor. Each stage answers one question, pulls context from EIR, and leaves a record the engineer can inspect.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps steps-numbered">
        {gcsChain.map(([n, d]) => <li><strong>{['CAM', 'BDI', 'PPM'].includes(n) ? <Term t={n} /> : n}</strong><span>{d}</span></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="display" style="font-size:var(--step-3)">Knowledge and assurance</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><b>EIR</b> keeps permanent knowledge apart from temporary reasoning. Its repository, the <Term t="ACR" />, holds engineering knowledge, this aircraft's history and technology knowledge. Information Intelligence assembles just the context a stage needs into working memory.</p>
        <p><b>Sentinel</b> sits outside both. The operational side watches model performance and drift and controls versions; the knowledge side watches for conflicting or outdated documents. Nothing changes without validation and controlled approval. Physics is treated as fixed knowledge.</p>
        <p><b>A new aircraft does not need years of failures first.</b> Its engineering representation starts from documents, configuration and physics, and grows as it flies.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><a class="next-link" href="/digital-twin/"><span>Next</span><strong>Digital twin</strong></a></div>
</Base>
<style>
  .arch { display: grid; gap: var(--s-5); align-items: stretch; }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .arch { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; } }
  .arch-col { border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: var(--surface); padding: var(--s-5); }
  .arch-h { font-stretch: var(--wide); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--step-1); margin-bottom: var(--s-4); }
  .arch-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }
  .arch-list li { padding: var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); position: relative; }
  .arch-list li + li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0.2rem; top: -0.45rem; width: 1px; height: 0.9rem; background: var(--line-strong); }
  .arch-list li.key { font-weight: 640; }
  .arch-link { display: grid; place-items: center; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .arch-link span { border-top: 1px dashed var(--line-strong); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line-strong); padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-4); }
  .steps { list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .steps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 14rem) 1fr; gap: var(--s-5); padding: var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .steps strong { font-weight: 620; }
  .steps span { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .steps-numbered { counter-reset: s; }
  .steps-numbered strong::before { counter-increment: s; content: counter(s, decimal-leading-zero) '  '; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 400; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .steps li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.2rem; } }
</style>
